[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3029370502","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108216#issuecomment-3029370502","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108216","id":3029370502,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60kIaG","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T21:26:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T21:37:19Z","body":"> where the collection (belonging to `SceneState`) is shallowly duplicated\r\n\r\nProbably worth pointing out that while this is now (hopefully) consistent between the typed and untyped case, you can easily find yourself in similar trouble if you have a collection of objects instead, since the duplication is not a deep one.\r\n\r\n~~I feel like it probably should be changed to a deep duplication for both cases, so as to not mess with the `SceneState` stuff, but I can't say I understand the ramifications of changing that, other than performance.~~\r\n\r\nEDIT: I totally forgot about `resource_local_to_scene`. However, even when enabling that for the objects in the collection it doesn't seem to have the intended effect, in either the untyped or typed case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3029370502/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3029417762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108216#issuecomment-3029417762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108216","id":3029417762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60kT8i","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T21:49:01Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T21:56:34Z","body":"> However, even when enabling that for the objects in the collection it doesn't seem to have the intended effect, in either the untyped or typed case.\r\n\r\nAt the risk of complicating this PR further, I threw in a fix for this as well, since it seemed very related, as `SceneState::setup_resources_in_array` and `SceneState::setup_resources_in_dictionary` were being called on the original `SceneState` instance of the c